# AvaKit token-gated project rules

Content is gated behind ownership of an access-pass NFT (`balanceOf(address) > 0`).

## Gate pattern

```ts
// Component body (hooks are not called inside callbacks or after an await):
const { address } = useAvaAccount(); // the visitor
const { read, write } = useContract({ address: passAddress, abi }); // the access-pass contract
// Effect or handler:
const balance = (await read("balanceOf", [address])) as bigint;
const hasAccess = balance > 0n; // only render gated content when true
```

- A pending or failed read is **unknown**, not "no pass". Keep the demo's `Gate` state
  (`checking` | `error` | `ready`): reset it to `checking` when the account or contract changes,
  show the error with a retry instead of the locked view, and ignore answers for a previous account.
- Deploy the pass: `useAvaDeploy().deploy({ abi, bytecode })` (artifact in `lib/nft-artifact.ts`),
  then `useDeployedContract(...).remember(address)` (`lib/deployed-contract.ts`) so a reload keeps it.
- Mint a pass: `write("mint", [])`.
- To gate on a different token, point `useContract` at its address/ABI and adjust the threshold.

## Contract

- `contracts/src/AvaKitNFT.sol` (minimal, self-contained). Recompile: `cd contracts && forge build`, then update `lib/nft-artifact.ts`.

## UI

- shadcn/ui only; `@avakit/react` components are shadcn-styled.
- Black & white only for now; dark/light via next-themes; both must work.
- Animations: Framer Motion or GSAP only.

## Test AVAX

- On Fuji, `app/providers.tsx` passes `faucetUrl` to `<AvaKitProvider>`: the temporary wallet is
  funded when it connects, any other empty wallet through `useFaucet().fund()`. The default is
  AvaKit's shared Fuji faucet: rate-limited (one small drip per address per day, plus an hourly cap
  per IP address), paid for by the AvaKit maintainer, for first runs only — not for a product.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_AVAKIT_FAUCET_URL` = your own faucet's `/fund` URL (Worker in `services/faucet` of
  the AvaKit repository), or `off`. Never pass a faucet URL on a chain other than Fuji.
- `components/funding.tsx` (`useFunding()`, `<FundingNotice />`) shows the funding state and the
  fallback (the official faucet needs a free Builder Hub sign-in). Disable transaction buttons only
  while `funding.isEmpty` — an unknown balance is not an empty one.
- Never call `fund()` on mount: the provider already asks for the temporary wallet and reports it
  through `useFaucet()`, and a second request is refused as "funded recently". `status: "success"`
  means the faucet sent the drip, not that it arrived — wait for a non-zero balance.

## Safety

- Client-side gating is illustrative — verify ownership server-side for real secrets (SIWE + API).
- Deploying/minting costs gas; a new wallet is funded by the faucet (see "Test AVAX").
- Default chain is Fuji testnet; mainnet requires explicit opt-in.
